  "worked_solution": "Let $f(x)=\\sqrt[3]{-6-3x}.$ Let's sketch the graph of $y=f(x):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14253135/assets/481fd6651401a37e221648026506b508f3ba9984a0637c2f2219c52a5f561b23.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the function decreases without bound as $x$ increases. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x)=-\\infty .\n$$",
